text:
elaine: FYI support escalated a puzzler: client did a model swap from `redwood-embed-v1` -> `redwood-embed-v2` at the same time they rotated presigned upload URLs. After the swap, embeddings calls returned 401s for a short period. Text generation calls were unaffected.

samir: Interesting. Did they also rotate API keys or only the presigned S3 URLs?

elaine: Only presigned URLs for user uploads. They updated the model field in their batch job immediately after rotating the URLs. The failing error was `401 Unauthorized: signature mismatch` coming from the embeddings route.

ben: That implies the request body included the old signed URL and backend auth expected a different signature. Could be a client-side cache or a stale reference in the job.

tay: Our routing + auth flow is: front-door validates auth, then routes to model backend. Embeddings path should hit same auth layer as text-gen. If text-gen passed, then maybe embeddings service validates a user-upload signature as part of its payload checks.

elaine: They sent this sanitized curl example:

```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/embeddings \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer sk-prod-REDACTED" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"redwood-embed-v2","input":"...","user_upload_url":"https://s3.aws/signed?X-Amz-Signature=OLDSIG"}'
```

elaine: When the client requested a fresh presigned URL and retried, the requests succeeded.

samir: Sounds like a race: model swap + rotation of short-lived credentials. Docs should explicitly warn about this.

ben: Proposed docs change: add a new subsection under "Model swap checklist" called "Short-lived credentials and referenced assets" with guidance:
- Issue new presigned URLs and ensure clients refresh references before bulk model swaps
- Invalidate or expire client-side caches of presigned links
- Run a small end-to-end smoke test per user after rotating signatures

tay: Also mention older SDK behavior: some pre-1.0 clients send a `model_hint` header. During swaps, recommend sending canonical model names and avoid optimistic hints to reduce routing ambiguity.

samir: For SDK migration guide: add a sample retry/backoff snippet that catches 401 on embeddings and re-fetches a presigned URL then retries once or with exponential backoff for ~30-60s.

elaine: Draft JS snippet I'm planning to include:

```js
// 1) request a presigned upload URL from app server
const { url } = await api.fetch('/uploads/presign', { userId });
// 2) upload the file
await fetch(url, { method: 'PUT', body: file });
// 3) call embeddings with the returned URL
try {
  await redwood.embeddings.create({ model: 'redwood-embed-v2', input, user_upload_url: url });
} catch (err) {
  if (err.status === 401) {
    // refresh presigned url and retry once
    const { url: freshUrl } = await api.fetch('/uploads/presign', { userId });
    await fetch(freshUrl, { method: 'PUT', body: file });
    await redwood.embeddings.create({ model: 'redwood-embed-v2', input, user_upload_url: freshUrl });
  } else throw err;
}
```

elaine: I'll add wording: "If your deployment rotates presigned credentials or short-lived tokens, invalidate stored references before performing a model swap."

ben: I'll add a migration smoke test: simulate stale presigned URLs, expect client to refresh and succeed within a minute.

samir: Also add a short note in the SDK breaking changes doc: mention that embedded assets that use short-lived signatures may cause transient 401s during infra changes, and recommend the snippet above.

tay: Can we add a pointer to runtime routing doc for teams who rely on model hints? Say: "Prefer explicit model names during migrations; see runtime routing for how model hints are resolved" and link to internal runtime doc.

elaine: Action items:
- elaine: open docs PR with the new subsection + curl and JS snippets, include support case link  target: EOD today
- samir: add retry/backoff example and update SDK migration guide to call out 401 semantics
- tay: add line about `model_hint` and add runtime routing doc link
- ben: add smoke test to the migration harness to cover stale presigned URL scenario

docs-bot: PR opened: github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/2279 by elaine  draft: "Model swap: short-lived credentials & embeddings race condition" :eyes:

elaine: pinging @samir @tay for quick review. I'll also prepare an internal SRE checklist to run a single-user post-swap smoke per region.

samir: Good catch by support, thanks.

tay: quick copy nits only, looks good.

ben: I'll follow up with the test PR.

elaine: Thanks everyone. Will close the thread when PR merges. :white_check_mark:
